main={39:('ISSN Manual P11/P17 supplies the exact combined distinguishing relation: specific continuing resource, defined medium, permanent unique standardized key title. DOI may identify that object but does not define this ISSN-specific key-title linkage. ISBN identifies a monographic product/form, OCLC a database record. The prompt now contains the discriminant formerly missing; one key ISSN.',[ISSN,MAN,DOI,ISBN,OCLC]),40:('DOI FAQ§8 permits any physical, digital or abstract entity, and §1 requires an RA service for assignment. ISBN covers monographic publications and separately available publication portions, not arbitrary entities; ISSN specializes in continuing resources/key titles; OCLC numbers WorldCat records. Broad any-entity scope is in the prompt itself, so ISBN scholarly/digital overlap no longer supplies a second key.',[DOI,ISBN,ISSN,MAN,OCLC])}
expl={39:('Two sentences: unique continuing resource in defined medium, then permanent standardized unique key-title relationship. Exact Manual P11/P17 facts; FAQ corroborates title standardization and distinguishing qualifiers. It does not claim DOI is unable to name a serial object.',[MAN,ISSN]),40:('Two sentences accurately paraphrase FAQ§8 any entity and primary intended community-sharing/IP-management uses. No assertion that these are the only uses; no invented DOI restriction to scholarly or digital objects.',[DOI])}
notes={39:[('DOI FAQ§8 explicitly any physical/digital/abstract entity and scholarly research among uses. «Например» preserves its broader construction/entertainment scope.',[DOI]),('FAQ explicitly gives eight-character structure, modulo11 check calculation and X if computed value is10. «Восемь знаков» now includes X correctly; no claim of eight decimal digits.',[ISSN,MAN]),('OCLC L417 assigns unique control number to each bibliographic WorldCat record and prohibits changing it. Note has both precise entity and invariant.',[OCLC]),('ISBN L27/L35/L40/L44 supports monographic title/edition/format and separate forms. It does not assert that separately available chapters/issues/articles in L43 can never carry ISBN.',[ISBN])],40:[('OCLC L417 gives each clause: unique record number, immutable control number, assignment after Produce or Update Holdings. This is a precise WorldCat workflow fact, not universal identifier behavior.',[OCLC]),('FAQ§1 expressly says RAs collect metadata, assign DOI names, offer reference linking or metadata lookup; §5 qualifies RA/domain lookup versus absent system-wide search. «Могут» avoids requiring every agency to offer every service.',[DOI]),('ISBN L35/L40 supports monographic publication/title/edition/format, L44 separate product forms. No exclusive ban on independently sold chapters/issues/articles is asserted.',[ISBN]),('Manual P11/P17 specifies continuing resource in defined medium and permanently linked unique standardized key title. FAQ confirms standardized key-title disambiguation; this is not DOI-wide all-entity scope.',[MAN,ISSN])]}
plaus={39:[('DOI is plausible because it can name scholarly/serial objects.','Its broad object capacity does not define a continuing-resource identifier permanently linked to a unique standardized key title; that conjunction selects ISSN.'),('ISSN is a familiar serial identifier among bibliography systems.','Only ISSN has the specified continuing-resource/medium/key-title standard linkage.'),('OCLC is plausible because WorldCat records describe serial publications and their titles.','A bibliographic record control number is not the specified continuing-resource/key-title standard code.'),('ISBN is a nearby international publication number; separate issues/articles can have one.','Monographic product/title/edition/form scope lacks the continuing-resource/medium/permanent key-title linkage.')],40:[('OCLC is plausible as a machine-assigned persistent number in a large bibliographic system.','Its object is a WorldCat record, not any physical/digital/abstract entity through DOI-style RA services.'),('DOI is plausible as an agency-assigned identifier used for many objects.','FAQ§1+§8 exactly matches the prompt conjunction, making this the unique key.'),('ISBN is plausible because agencies assign it to printed and digital scholarly books.','That overlap was the INITIAL defect; current prompt requires any physical/digital/abstract entity, beyond publication products and portions.'),('ISSN is plausible as another international identifier with network assignment.','Continuing-resource/medium/key-title specialization is narrower than any-entity assignment.') ]}
extras={39:('Eight characters including a check character and possible terminal X for computed10. Prompt asks continuing-resource/medium/key-title relation, so numerical structure/X is genuinely additional.',[ISSN,MAN]),40:('Metadata collection plus optional reference linking and metadata lookup services. Prompt already states RA assignment and any-entity scope; those repeated facts are not counted as extra. Additional agency services are concrete and useful.',[DOI])}
